{
 "razonamiento": "The architecture shows an agent-facing web application migration to serverless on AWS. Static assets for the single-page application (SPA) are hosted in S3 and delivered via CloudFront to the user/agents (represented as UserCompanyAgent, drawn as b7). Dynamic API calls route to API Gateway, which delegates authorization to a Lambda authorizer and routes requests to a Python backend Lambda. This backend Lambda interacts with DynamoDB for caching user information and connects to legacy Tomcat applications running on EC2 for unmigrated functionality. All 14 visual lines represent bidirectional request/response interactions across the two primary workflows (static site retrieval and API request processing).",
 "nombre": "Serverless Modernization with API Gateway, Lambda, and Legacy EC2 Integration",
